==English==

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|fro|requerre}} (whence Modern {{cog|fr|requérir}}), from {{uder|en|la|requīrō||to require, seek, ask for|lit=to seek back}}, from {{m|la|re-||back; again}} + {{m|la|quaerō||to seek|pos=whence {{m|en|query}}}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈkwaɪə/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈkwaɪɹ/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈkwʌɪɹ/|a=CA,idle-idol split}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-require.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-require.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪə(ɹ)|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|re|quire}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[demand]], to insist upon (having); to call for authoritatively. {{defdate|from 14th c.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1998|author=Joan Wolf|title=The Gamble|publisher=Warner Books
|passage="I am Miss Newbury," I announced, "and I '''require''' to be shown to my room immediately, if you please."}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=29 December 2009|author=Vikram Dodd|journal=The Guardian
|passage=‘Regrettably, I have concluded, after considering the matter over Christmas{{nb...}}, that I can no longer maintain the high standard of service I '''require''' of myself, meet the demands of office and cope with the pressures of public life, without my health deteriorating further.’}}
# Naturally to demand (something) as [[indispensable]]; to [[need]], to call for as necessary. {{defdate|from 15th c.}}
#* {{RQ:Time|date=5 June 1972|title=Aid for Aching Heads
|passage=Chronic pain is occasionally a sign of a very serious problem, like brain tumors, and can '''require''' surgery.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=7 February 2009|author=Julian Borger|journal=The Guardian
|passage=A weapon small enough to put on a missile would '''require''' uranium enriched to more than 90% U-235.}}
# To [[demand]] (of someone) to do something. {{defdate|from 18th c.}}
#: {{syn|en|provide|}}
#: {{ux|en|It is '''require'''d (of me) that I give evidence in court.}}
#* {{RQ:Time|date=29 June 1970|title=Compulsory Midi
|passage=After Aug 3 all salesgirls will be '''required''' to wear only one style of skirt while on duty: the midi.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=5 December 2007|author=Allegra Stratton|title=Smith to ban non-EU unskilled immigrants from working in UK|journal=The Guardian
|passage=The government would like to '''require''' non-British fiances who wish to marry a British citizen to sit an English test.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To [[ask]] (someone) for something; to [[request]]; to [[beseech]]. {{defdate|14th|17th c.}}
#* {{RQ:Malory Le Morte Darthur|book=IX|chapter=XI|page=355|text=I '''requyre''' yow lete vs be sworne to gyders that neuer none of vs shalle after this day haue adoo with other, and there with alle syre Tristram and sire Lamorak sware that neuer none of hem shold fyghte ageynst other nor for wele, nor for woo.|t=I '''request''' that you let us be sworn together, so that neither of us shall ever again after this day have ado with the other, and [[therewithal]] Sir Tristan and Sir Lamorak swore that neither of them would fight against the other ever again, whether ''for well or for woe'' [i.e. for good or bad reasons].}}
#* {{RQ:Tyndale NT|Mark|V|passage=I '''requyre''' the in the name of god, that thou torment me nott.|t=I '''beseech''' thee, for God's sake, do not torment me.}}

